{"Title":"An Act relative to tuition waivers for children raised by a grandparent or other relative ","BillNumber":"H1257","DocketNumber":"HD2533","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"PJD1","Name":"Paul J. Donato","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PJD1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T14:24:18.39"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"PJD1","Name":"Paul J. Donato","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PJD1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T14:24:18.39"},{"Id":"CRF1","Name":"Christopher Richard Flanagan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CRF1","ResponseDate":"2023-05-02T11:20:22.5966667"},{"Id":"S_G1","Name":"Sean Garballey","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/S_G1","ResponseDate":"2023-10-17T10:45:05.0766667"},{"Id":"PJK1","Name":"Patrick Joseph Kearney","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PJK1","ResponseDate":"2023-10-20T12:16:28.84"},{"Id":"jml0","Name":"Jason M. Lewis","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jml0","ResponseDate":"2023-10-25T12:31:15.38"},{"Id":"JBA1","Name":"Jennifer Balinsky Armini","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JBA1","ResponseDate":"2023-10-27T12:48:25.1766667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H1257/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Donato of Medford, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 1257) of Paul J. Donato relative to tuition waivers for children raised by a grandparent or other relative.  Higher Education.","DocumentText":"\tSection 19 of chapter 15A of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the ninth paragraph the following paragraph:-\r\n\tThe program shall provide tuition and fee waivers for any resident of the commonwealth who has been the subject of a legal guardianship pursuant to section 5-201 of chapter 190B of the General Laws and who, upon reaching the age of 18 or upon enrolling in a Massachusetts institution of higher education, is living with a grandparent or other relative, including any person related by consanguinity, marriage or affinity except for a parent. The commonwealth, not the institutions of public higher education, shall bear the cost of these waivers after all reimbursements from the federal government have been exhausted.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J29","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J29"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}